WEBVTT

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.610
Sandbag ni

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.610
On the sandbag,

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:40.830
He's done it! He's done it!

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:42.790
Two minutes and forty seconds into the fourth round!

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:46.440
Rikiishi's uppercut has finally hit Yabuki square in the jaw!

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.790
Yabuki's down! Can he get back up?

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.790
Bro Joe! Get up! Quick!

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.300
Hang in there, Yabuki-kun...

00:01:58.090 --> 00:02:00.180
Joe! Get up! Get up!

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.730
And Yabuki's up! And on the count of nine!

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.240
He grabbed the ropes and pulled himself up!

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.740
H-He may be up, but I wouldn't call that standing...

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.740
A-Are you all right, Yabuki?

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:48.550
Now this is cruel! Rikiishi's throwing an uppercut at the reeling Yabuki!

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:59.490
And just look at that! How great of Rikiishi!

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:06.150
That's the bell. Back to your corners.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:11.410
He swung the uppercut before the bell! It wouldn't have been a foul had he landed it!

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:16.550
But still, Rikiishi stopped his uppercut an inch under Yabuki's jaw, just as the bell rang!

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:24.010
Hey, Joe! Come on!

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:27.640
Was that move to show his confidence in his victory?

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.990
Rikiishi truly is a fair fighter!

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:33.380
Yabuki! You're lucky! That would've put you down!

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:34.560
<i>You really got saved by the bell!</i>

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.070
Rikiishi! Finish him next round!

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.050
They're all right.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.070
You still have luck on your side.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:44.950
If that bell had been a split-second late, you'd be out.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:46.800
Here. Have some water.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.670
Wh-What was that sound?

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.720
Look! His tooth broke!

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.880
B-But that's one of his molars!

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.500
Joe, give up.

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:18.540
The match is over. If this goes on any longer...

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:29.680
But I guess you're not gonna accept that, are you?

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.510
All right, listen up, Joe.

00:04:34.980 --> 00:04:37.650
In a way, your life ended back there.

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:41.670
Why don't you just forget about what comes next, and try real boxing?

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.170
Real boxing?

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:46.610
Yes. Real boxing!

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:49.140
Quit that offbeat tactic of hanging your arms limp at your sides!

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:56.180
Put up a tight guard, and use normal attacks, starting with jabs and throwing straights and hooks!

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:58.460
Try doing that with deathly resolve.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:01.760
If that doesn't work, then we'll accept defeat.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:02.150
Well?

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.340
What do you say, Joe?

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.900
Go out with a frontal attack!

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.160
Got it?

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:09.700
Seconds out!

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.160
You got it?

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:17.340
I already thought that was the only way.{}

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.260
Now, what could this mean?

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.250
Yabuki's put up a tight guard!

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:02.750
This is the first time Yabuki's put his hands up to guard himself in his professional career!

00:06:06.130 --> 00:06:08.560
This is a sign of submission.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:14.260
Joe the Brawler's admitting that his wild fighting spirit is helpless before Rikiishi's honed techniques.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.210
It's a cruel submission.

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:24.230
Joe! Remember! For the Sake of Tomorrow #1, #2, and #3!

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:27.240
For the Sake of Tomorrow #1, #2, and #3...

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:40.730
Cut it out, cut it out! That's out of character!

00:06:40.730 --> 00:06:43.380
You can only box from the No Guard stance!

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.120
Do us all a favor and let Rikiishi pummel you!

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.870
Oh, no! Old man, Rikiishi's breaking through his guard!

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:01.690
You moron! Now what are you gonna do?

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:23.570
Told you so! That guard didn't do you any good!

00:07:23.570 --> 00:07:25.840
Come on, Yabuki! Get up, get up!

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.720
Is he getting up?

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.870
Joe's guard saved him!

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.890
Rikiishi's punch lost power because it had to go through his guard!

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:43.150
He can get up after that!

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:44.360
Joe can get up!

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:20.440
Look! Not only is he back up, but he's still throwing punches!

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:21.390
Wh-What the hell?

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.830
Joe! Go for it!

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.620
His stamina is just beyond reason!

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:49.060
Even after taking so much damage, Yabuki is still punching aggressively!

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:52.030
No, I wouldn't be so sure. The damage is taking its toll on Yabuki.

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:53.840
Take a good look at his feet and eyes.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:02.990
Yes, his eyes are hollow, and his footwork's quite dull compared to Rikiishi's.

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:05.770
Yes, and even the guard he just put up

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:08.410
is starting to sink!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.150
Slip! That's a slip!

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:15.650
Joe!

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:25.750
Joe!

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.510
Hey, Joe! Pull yourself together!

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:38.650
It appears Yabuki is on the verge of losing consciousness!

00:09:38.650 --> 00:09:41.680
It doesn't look like he can carry on the match anymore.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:46.480
You said it. Besides, we'd already figured the match was over by the fourth round.

00:09:46.910 --> 00:09:50.220
He barely managed to get up before the count-out,

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:53.980
but if I were the referee, I would've declared Rikiishi's victory then and there!

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.990
Joe, can you stand? Can you?

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.000
And the sixth round begins!

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:13.460
Can the half-dead Yabuki last to the end of the round?

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.540
Hey, hey, enough is enough, Coach!

00:10:36.540 --> 00:10:37.900
How long are you gonna force him through this?

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.520
Old man! Old man!

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:48.250
Dammit...

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:52.130
Make them stop! He's gonna die!

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:57.130
Throw in the towel, you murderer! Hurry!

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.370
Throw in the towel!

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:03.260
Hurry up! Stop this! Hey!{added by tlc}

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:09.000
No! I can't do that!

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:12.230
No matter how many times he collapses, it's not about winning or losing anymore!

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:17.230
Look! Joe's still attacking!

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:19.740
He's giving it all he has!

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:39.050
Enough is enough!

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:42.350
Referee, the fight's settled! Stop the match!

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:44.890
Same goes for you, Rikiishi! Quit trying to drag this out!

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.290
Finish this already!

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:48.650
Torturing your opponent's pretty much a crime!

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:50.180
Keep with it, Rikiishi!

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.880
Rikiishi's not trying to drag it out.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.310
He's getting exhausted!

00:11:54.310 --> 00:12:00.650
He's panicking! His deadly weight loss has caused him to lose stamina quicker than ever!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:16.880
Rikiishi-kun!

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.720
He did it!

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:32.890
You did it, Yabuki! Way to go, Yabuki!

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.010
Get to a neutral corner!

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:58.920
I'm fine. I can keep going.

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:04.400
Rikiishi shakes his head and stands up!

00:13:04.400 --> 00:13:06.670
Still, wasn't that quite a strange way to fall?

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:09.550
Perhaps he had a slight concussion?

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:13.930
Keep it up, Joe! Don't waste this chance! Go get him!

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:15.480
Get him!

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.020
O-Old man, look!

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:34.680
H-How could this be? That's...

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:47.360
What a bizarre sight this is!

00:13:47.360 --> 00:13:49.750
Of all things, Rikiishi's using the No Guard stance!

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:52.760
Has he lost his sense of judgment?

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:59.730
No, we've seen since this match began that Rikiishi's completely researched all of Yabuki's moves.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:02.270
This may be some form of horrifying strategy!

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:03.750
No!

00:14:09.310 --> 00:14:13.570
You've gotta be kidding me! What's he gonna do with my trademarked No Guard?

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:18.460
Joe! Don't go in there! Stop!

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:22.960
He's trying to repeat the Wolf match!

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:26.130
If you're on the receiving end of Rikiishi's Triple Cross Counter,

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.510
you'll be dead for sure!

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:42.830
Th-That son of a bitch!

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:45.190
H-He just thought up something deadly!

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:05.170
Wh-What's going on? I never used to be afraid of shit, so why am I so frightened by him?

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:17.430
That's it!

00:15:28.940 --> 00:15:31.950
And Yabuki's gone back to hanging his arms by his side!

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:34.240
This is becoming quite a serious match!

00:15:37.310 --> 00:15:40.560
How about that, Rikiishi? Now we're even!

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:41.750
So what'll it be?

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:44.640
Now this is good! It's a No Guard faceoff!

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.290
This is what I'm talking about!{added by tlc}

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:06.940
Joe, I gotta take off my hat to your wild instincts!

00:16:07.370 --> 00:16:10.220
That was good! That really was good!

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:13.210
You really made Rikiishi jump back there!

00:16:13.690 --> 00:16:17.510
Only two rounds left! Keep on your toes, all right?

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:18.450
Yeah.

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:33.810
Neither fighter is moving a muscle!

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:36.640
Or perhaps I should say that they can't move?

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:39.670
This is just like a stalemate in chess!

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:42.770
One wrong move could be fatal!

00:16:45.240 --> 00:16:47.430
Come on, fight, you two!

00:16:47.430 --> 00:16:49.440
Fight! Fight, fight!

00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:53.700
Quit trying to stir up shit, Mr. Referee...

00:16:54.080 --> 00:16:56.820
I'm the one who's losing his patience here!

00:16:57.170 --> 00:17:01.100
The reason I'm just staring him down

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.970
is because I see a terrifying conclusion ahead of me!

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:14.470
Ishida-san, back in his match with Wolf, wasn't Wolf knocked out after he charged?

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:21.160
Yes, and not only that, he fractured his jaw in multiple places and had to leave the ring for good!

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:25.480
It'll... It'll probably be Yabuki-kun who makes the first move.

00:17:27.560 --> 00:17:33.440
I think so, too. Rikiishi-kun has probably figured Yabuki-kun's short fuse into his calculations.

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:37.450
Joe! Please, don't make the first move!

00:18:08.480 --> 00:18:11.770
What's wrong, you two? Fight! Fight!

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:14.350
Start fighting! Fight! Fight!

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:16.030
Fight!

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:18.610
Fight!

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:21.740
Now, fight! Fight! Fight!

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:23.030
Fight! Fight!

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:26.040
He's telling us to fight. Come on, Rikiishi!

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:19.800
I don't care who starts! Just start fighting!

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:21.010
Fight!

00:19:21.010 --> 00:19:24.010
It won't be much of a match if this keeps up, right, Ishida-san?

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:30.290
Hey, hey, are you still doing that staring contest?

00:19:30.290 --> 00:19:32.670
This is the final round!

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:33.980
Cut it out!

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:39.140
We didn't pay this high ticket price just to see you looking each other in the eye!

00:19:39.140 --> 00:19:41.350
Yeah! Gimme back my money!

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:44.990
You thieves!

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:47.120
Shut up!

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:50.630
Are you gonna take away a boxer's life in the ring just for an entry fee?

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:51.500
Now keep it down!

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:56.770
Screw your "life in the ring"! We came to see a fight, not a goddamn staring contest!

00:19:56.770 --> 00:20:02.080
Cut it out! We don't need people who can't accept anything but knockouts! Now get lost!

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:05.260
What's that, one-eye? Is that how you talk to a fan?

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:11.600
So what if you're a fan? If you don't keep it down, I'll punch your...

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:11.600
<i>Old man! Don't let them rile you up!</i>

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:15.460
I don't like how cowardly Yabuki is, either!

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:19.610
That's right! If he doesn't come out swinging, Rikiishi will win by points!

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:24.280
You think you can lose by points as long as you don't get hurt?

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:27.810
You don't care if you break your knockout streak?

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:31.660
I thought you'd have the drive to risk a little injury to beat Rikiishi to a pulp!

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:33.990
I misjudged you, Yabuki!

00:20:33.990 --> 00:20:35.670
You assholes!

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:39.800
How about I shut your mouth for you?

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:42.800
What? Wanna fight, one-eye?

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:54.270
If the bell rings, I'll lose by points!

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:56.020
But if I strike first...

00:20:56.780 --> 00:20:57.730
But wait!

00:20:58.220 --> 00:21:03.720
In my match with Wolf, I was able to pull off a Triple Cross Counter because Wolf's Double was too slow!

00:21:04.410 --> 00:21:09.030
But my punch isn't anything like Wolf's!

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:12.030
Don't move, Joe! Don't you dare make a move!

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:15.190
I said don't move!

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:19.570
That's it. I'm not being conceited. I <i>am</i> better than him!

00:21:19.940 --> 00:21:26.810
Even if Rikiishi tries a Triple Cross, logically, my Double will hit him a split second quicker!

00:21:27.290 --> 00:21:31.560
And if it's strong enough, Rikiishi will collapse before he can land the Triple!

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:37.560
Now!

00:21:37.560 --> 00:21:38.560
No!

00:21:38.910 --> 00:21:40.510
And Yabuki's charging ahead!

00:21:45.440 --> 00:21:47.850
And he throws a powerful left straight!

00:21:48.290 --> 00:21:49.090
There it is!

00:21:51.740 --> 00:21:52.830
I just gotta repel it

00:21:53.390 --> 00:21:55.330
and end this with my Double Cross!

00:23:09.870 --> 00:23:13.480
It's over. It's all over.

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:25.340
Their intense battle is finally over.

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:29.050
And Joe and Rikiishi are about to exchange their true handshake of friendship.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:33.490
But because of the strict weight loss compounded by the intensity of the fight,

00:23:33.490 --> 00:23:35.960
Rikiishi collapses on the spot.

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:38.710
Though in defeat, Joe has no regrets.

00:23:39.360 --> 00:23:41.870
He now thinks upon Rikiishi's greatness.

00:23:42.810 --> 00:23:47.460
But then, news of Rikiishi's death comes suddenly to Joe!

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:50.520
Joe is dumbfounded by the unthinkable news!

00:23:51.270 --> 00:23:55.070
Rikiishi... The same Rikiishi that launched the mighty uppercut...

00:23:55.650 --> 00:23:57.080
Rikiishi is dead!

00:23:58.280 --> 00:24:01.150
As Joe screams out in agony,

00:24:02.100 --> 00:24:04.040
who will understand how he feels!?

00:24:18.070 --> 00:24:21.110
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:18.070 --> 00:24:21.110
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:24.950
Oira boxer

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:24.950
I am a boxer.

00:24:25.740 --> 00:24:32.710
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:24:25.740 --> 00:24:32.710
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:24:34.420 --> 00:24:38.380
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:24:34.420 --> 00:24:38.380
Everyone says that I am merciless.

00:24:38.380 --> 00:24:40.420
Tsuki ni hoete hitori

00:24:38.380 --> 00:24:40.420
Howling at the moon alone.

00:24:42.510 --> 00:24:46.640
Oyanashi yadonashi no na mo nai boxer wa

00:24:42.510 --> 00:24:46.640
A parentless, homeless, nameless boxer

00:24:46.640 --> 00:24:49.640
Kusari wo kamikitta Yeah Yeah!

00:24:46.640 --> 00:24:49.640
has bitten off his chains! Yeah, yeah!

00:24:51.350 --> 00:24:54.270
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:51.350 --> 00:24:54.270
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:55.480 --> 00:24:57.980
Oira boxer

00:24:55.480 --> 00:24:57.980
I am a boxer.

00:24:59.110 --> 00:25:06.240
Asahi ga noboru yo otoko no mune ni {removed the Woo, but otherwise japanese is unchanged - Reed}

00:24:59.110 --> 00:25:06.240
The morning sun rises upon the hearts of men!
